w those supporting characters will  play into the story in a bit we learned  a while back though that this series  will be set in the 50s which is very  interesting looking at this concept art  you can see that clearly with this  idyllic 50s era suburban attire two  things to note here one this looks a  whole lot like Tom King and Gabriel  Walter's vision series from 2015 this  series followed vision as he built his  own nuclear family and tried to live a  suburban life fun fact his wife's brain  patterns were copied from Wanda's sounds  like a super healthy way to get over  your ex you can see some of that style  from the comic being mirrored in this  promotional art also we have writer Tom  Kane weighing in with this post this  looks an awful lot like the Dick Van  Dyke Show  sitcoms of that era I used that  succumbed specifically based on the  footage that was shown at d23 according  to the attendees at that conference the  promotion for one division showed clips  from Civil War and infinity war with one  and vision together along with clips  from the Dick Van Dyke Show specifically  scenes with Dick Van Dyke and Mary Tyler  Moore questioning their relationship  these scenes intercut with Wanda and  vision definitely leave you with a sense  of distrust whether the events are  actually happening and questioning what  is real but there's also transitioned us  to my favorite update this series is  gonna be the first sitcom in the MCU now  I know some of you may have grown on the  other side of this screen but think  about it one has gone through a lot in  her young life she grew up in a war-torn  country was experimented on by Hydra  lost her brother accidentally killed  civilians and Lagos had the Avengers and  the world turn on her and she loses her  Robo lover twice to Thanos and then gets  snapped out of existence after returning  she may be a wee bit interested into  looking to make her life a little bit  more simple  maybe she's able to create a false  reality with the help of her mental  manipulation powers telekinesis and  possibly reality slash probability  warping powers from the comics a reality  similar to a sitcom that she grew up  loving where the audience actively love  and appreciate the characters we see  on-screen where she can finally feel  accepted Elizabeth Olsen even joked  saying that the producers were deciding  if they wanted to add a laugh track or  not please the creators behind this show  have discussed that the facade will  collapse pretty quickly once the show  begins and turn into something truly  epic something that we come to expect  from the MCU now let's dive into what we  could be seeing in the series looking at  the concept art we see both of our  characters Wanda and vision in their  classic color schemes red for Wanda and  a mix of purple green and yellow for  vision but we've also got a haunting  shadow of their super selves with the  first appearance of Wanda's classic face  mask along with the mine stone or  possibly the solar jewel that absorbs  sunlight like in the comics right back  there on the wall you can see a little  bomb you'll also notice the idyllic 50s  coloring stops just outside the light  from the TV which seems to be giving off  some sort of scarlet witch's red energy  my theory is that Wanda is diving deep  into what she's capable of in the comic  events like house of M we seen Wanda  change all of reality to suit her will  she can manifest just about anything  into reality if she chooses to could she  possibly be creating a fake  in a real suburb that draws the  attention of her neighbors and possibly  the superhero community this could lead  to Jimmy woo former agent of shield  turned FBI agent teaming up with Darci  Lewis a grad student who has been  studying interdimensional energies with  Jane Foster and Erik Selvig to find out  what is going on in this quiet suburban  neighborhood this could also lead to  Monica Rambeau showing up to either gain  her abilities due to this reality  warping nonsense or could be the only  asset the Jimmy Wu has to take on the  Scarlet Witch also worth mentioning Wynn  Scarlet Witch created the house of  x-reality it was because she was powered  up by a demon named chip on a literal  devil  now Scarlet Witch has had run-ins with  Devils in the past so as vision actually  famously it was revealed that their tu  children were not created from Wanda's  powers no they were from Mephisto now  Mephisto is another popular devil in  Marvel Comics and I have a feeling that  he might be safer a larger story in the  MCU but I could 100% seeing wander using  the powers of something sinister to  bring back the one that she loves  another cool side note chick Don is tied  to the dark old evil mystical book from  Marvel Comics which appeared in a season  of agents of shield which they showed  was a book that was stolen from the  library of karma Taj the place where  Doctor Strange trained to be the  sorcerer supreme kind of cool how it all  comes together might make ages the  shield important so either one is  bringing vision literally back from the  dead or she's reaching into the  multiverse or an alternate timeline and  bringing vision back to this one this  could also be a good lead-in to Wanda  join Doctor Strange in multiverse of  madness she might be making a little bit  of a mess that she's gonna need to clean  up either way this is a solid way to  keep the stakes high for this series and  to make this really feel like a true  1950s era sitcom is to make it just not  a story about a happy couple in the  suburbs but a happy family  we know from interviews with the cast  and crew that they're pulling from  multiple comic storylines so why not  throw in Scarlet Witch envisions kids  Wiccan and speed these characters  famously popped up in the Young Avengers  comic and were confirmed by Scarlet  Witch to have the souls of their  children residing inside them you know  again turned out to be manifestations of  Mephisto so the whole thing is a little  confusing and convoluted but pretty cool  just have them be from another timeline  or from another universe similar to  what's going on with the Loki series on  super down if Wan division deals with  the multiverse like how Loki series is  going to be dealing with the alternate  Loki from another timeline that stole  the tesseract in  also these kids make it out of the  series add them to the mix with Kate  Bishop from the Hawkeye series and  Comicon from the Miss Marvel series and  you got yourself either a Young Avengers  series for a Champions team-up show in  the works what do you think could Scott  witch be manipulated by dark forces into  making a deal that brings a vision back  to the land of the living  could he be from an alternate timeline  an alternate universe let me know down  below don't forget to Like and subscribe  and follow me at San basher and send me  your thoughts and theories on Twitter  check our new rockstars a rogue theory  I'm on an episode of that and until next  time I'm Sam basher  [Music]

